  "integrity_notes": [
    "The 30 core features do not implement the complete 304-feature taxonomy.",
    "The current core-feature map has no core feature assigned to social_networks or style; those dimensions may have descriptive profiles only until a separately justified research extension exists.",
    "Reference means/prevalences/gaps are reproduced in the existing Table 16 source file; this registry does not create per-story numeric thresholds.",
    "The 33 reference patterns include alternative options within the same feature. They must never be counted as separate features or votes.",
    "No absence can be assigned a directional pattern by default.",
    "Numeric Table 16 values are not duplicated in this registry; validation reads the existing canonical Table 16 fixture to avoid multiple sources of truth.",
    "Pattern-level source provenance is direction-specific: AI-elevated patterns cite Tables 14 and 16; human-elevated patterns cite Tables 15 and 16. Table 16 is the source for all numerical values.",
    "Five features have no option-level numeric rows in Table 16 (Character Introduction, Dialogue Function, Mode of Resolution, Intertextual Strategy Types, Moral Polarity Toward Protagonist). Their directional labels are grounded in the canonical feature map and Tables 14/15; no numeric values are invented.",
    "Structural checks for this draft were performed ad hoc. A reproducible registry validator is not yet part of the repository or CI and will be a separate task.",
    "Legacy v0.2.3 canonical files may retain historical naming. This is documentary provenance, not a dependency or identity of StoryScope.",
    "historical_reference_pattern_id is added in registry version 0.1.2-draft as an explicit, validated selection of an existing reference pattern. It is not a new empirical claim: if an AI pattern exists, that pattern is selected; otherwise the human pattern is selected.",
    "For the current 30 features, historical_reference_pattern_id is mandatory and non-null. Future features without directional patterns may use null and then support only not_assessed relations.",
    "historical_reference_pattern_id is resolved by feature_id plus AnalysisRun.feature_registry_version; it is not duplicated in EvidenceRecord. Registry schema 1.1.0 adds this field; registry version 0.1.1-draft used schema 1.0.0.",
    "In the three bidirectional features, the historical reference is the AI pattern as a compatibility convention for historical comparison. This is not a hierarchy of quality between human and AI writing."
  ],
  "source_provenance_policy": {
    "ai_elevated_patterns": "Table 14 identifies the AI-elevated core feature/option; Table 16 supplies the human/AI values and gaps.",
    "human_elevated_patterns": "Table 15 identifies the human-elevated core feature/option; Table 16 supplies the human/AI values and gaps.",
    "table16_scope": "All 30 core features and their human/AI values and gaps are referenced from Table 16.",
    "prohibition": "Do not assign Tables 14 and 15 indiscriminately to every pattern; source attribution is direction-specific."
  }
}
